  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>The diagram shows a point source of sound S on the edge of a horizontal turntable that rotates about a vertical axis. The sound is detected using a small stationary frequency meter placed 0.78 m from the axis of the turntable. The turntable has a radius of 0.28 m. The linear speed of S is much less than the speed of sound.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The graph shows the variation of the detected frequency with rotation angle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span> for one revolution of the turntable.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a.i\"><p><strong>a.i</strong> State, on the diagram, the position of S for which the detected frequency is at a maximum. Label this position A. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a.ii\"><p><strong>a.ii</strong> Outline why this maximum frequency shift does not occur when θ = 90° or when θ = 270°. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Determine the angular speed of the turntable. The speed of sound is 330 m s<sup>−1</sup>. State an appropriate unit for your answer. [5]</p></section>"
  },
